    "title": "Altoona honored with namesake train from Norfolk Southern - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Derek Cestone ,\n10 hours ago\nALTOONA, Pa. (WTAJ) — Norfolk Southern unveiled a locomotive crafted and painted by its team in Altoona that honors the city’s rail legacy.\nThe train is the latest addition to Norfolk Southern’s Landmark Series. Each locomotive in the series bears the name of a city that had a significant impact on America’s rail history. The Altoona joins the Atlanta and the Birmingham as the third train in the series.\nThe engine was painted in Norfolk Southern’s Juniata Locomotive Shop in downtown Altoona.\nPhoto courtesy of Norfolk Southern “These locomotives aren’t just machines — they’re growth engines for the U.S. economy,” John Orr, Norfolk Southern Chief Operating Officer, said. “Each city we highlight is a center of economic activity that strengthens our network and drives commerce across the nation.”\nGet the latest news, weather forecasts and sports stories delivered straight to your inbox! Sign up for our newsletters . The engine is now in service and can be seen anywhere in Norfolk Southern’s network.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WTAJ - www.wtaj.com.\n1",
